"4b574a7a-bdad-59b8-aadb-22d876ef5c0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575541 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we convert from fluid ounces to cups. There are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup, so we divide the number of fluid ounces by $8:$     \n\n$$\n48÷8=6\n$$\n\nSo, $48$ fluid ounces is the same as $6$ cups. Now, to find the unit price per cup, we divide the total price by $6:$ \n\n$$\n11.52÷6=1.92\n$$\n\nTherefore, the juice costs $\\$1.92$ per cup." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575568 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575568 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68496" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575568 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575568 #edb/ref 1071 "Emma bought $2$ pounds of raisins for  $\\$4.80.$ What's the unit price per ounce?\n\nAssume that there are $16$ ounces in one pound." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575568 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7fb9ebfb-8542-5a5c-a420-5a62ca5ea273" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575568 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we convert from pounds to ounces. There are $16$ ounces in each pound, so we multiply the number of pounds  by $16:$  \n\n$$\n2\\times 16=32\n$$\n\nSo, $2$ pounds is the same as $32$ ounces. Now, to find the unit price per ounce, we divide the total price by $32:$\n\n$$\n4.80÷32=0.15\n$$\n\nTherefore, the raisins cost $\\$0.15$ per ounce." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575576 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575576 #edb/ref 1069 "q-354916" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575576 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575576 #edb/ref 1071 "Emily bought $1$ foot of gold wire and paid $\\$5.60$ for it. What's the unit price per yard?\n\nAssume that there are $3$ feet in one yard." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575576 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "947d34a3-027e-5d38-b8d1-e6f3a1b0d3d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575576 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that there are $3$ feet in each yard.  \n\nSince the price is $\\$5.60$ per foot, to find the price per yard, we multiply by $3:$\n\n$$\n5.60\\times 3=16.80\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gold wire costs $\\$16.80$ per yard." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575612 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575612 #edb/ref 1069 "q-354923" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575612 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575612 #edb/ref 1071 "A scientist bought $1$ fluid ounce of a chemical solution and paid $\\$1.60$ for it. What's the unit price per cup?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575612 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e3c42dde-368f-51a4-a96b-0c5d0e222f8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575612 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that there are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup.  \n\nSince the price is $\\$1.60$ per fluid ounce, to find the price per cup, we multiply by $8:$\n\n$$\n1.60\\times 8=12.80\n$$\n\nTherefore, the chemical solution costs $\\$12.80$ per cup." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575630 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186575687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575630 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "11472c15-674f-57c1-8bce-33ab7f36bb6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575630 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186575539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575640 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186575630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575640 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "222ef67b-ec25-5cef-b693-111a09425fec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575640 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186575568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575645 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186575678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575645 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a2423d0-c8dc-5183-b7f8-6ca7246149ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575645 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186575612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575678 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b27410e4-9002-576a-ac62-f2734f5665e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575678 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186575541 #edb/ref 17592